\paragraph{Hidden-state probe.}
A supervised logistic regression on mean-pooled final-layer hidden states at entity span positions achieves within-dataset AUROC of $0.920$ on Few-NERD and $0.957$ on CoNLL-2003 (5-fold CV ${\times}$ 3 seeds), exceeding multi-sample frequency agreement ($0.868$) from a single forward pass.
Cross-dataset transfer is weak: leave-one-dataset-out AUROC drops to $0.67$ (Few-NERD${\to}$CoNLL) and $0.56$ (CoNLL${\to}$Few-NERD), indicating dataset-specific rather than universal encoding of entity quality.

\paragraph{The introspection boundary.}
Entity quality is encoded in hidden representations (probe AUROC $0.92$) and recoverable from output distributions via multi-sample frequency agreement ($0.87$), yet inaccessible through prompt-based self-evaluation (ESJ AUROC $0.51$).
This is an introspection boundary, not an information deficit: self-verification fails not because the model lacks entity-level quality signals but because its generation interface cannot access them.

